## A turn at a glance

Every turn snapshots the creatures alive at its start, then walks them through
seven phases in a fixed order. Creatures born during a turn wait until the next
one before they act.

.mermaid caption:{The seven phases of a single simulation turn.}
    flowchart TD
        A([Turn start: snapshot]) --> B[1 - Movement]
        B --> C[2 - Combat]
        C --> D[3 - Remove the slain]
        D --> E[4 - Procreation]
        E --> F[5 - Starvation]
        F --> G[6 - Remove the starved]
        G --> H[7 - Food regrowth]
        H --> I([Turn end])

## Try it in one command

```sh
cargo run -- --turns 10 --delay-ms 0 --seed 42
```

With a seed, the same starting board always produces the same run, which makes
the simulation reproducible for tests, benchmarks, and bug reports.

## Project facts

| | |
|---|---|
| Language | Rust, edition 2024 |
| Binaries | `creature_life_cycle` (CLI), `gui` (Bevy) |
| GUI engine | Bevy 0.19 with `bevy_feathers` widgets |
| Configuration | TOML at `~/.config/creature_life_cycle/simulation.toml` |
| Repository | [andreashdez/creature_life_cycle](https://github.com/andreashdez/creature_life_cycle) |

